1
00:00:00,590 --> 00:00:04,090
(Leonard:)- Thank you.
- Honey, why did you get a loom?

2
00:00:04,928 --> 00:00:09,678
(Sheldon:)I was working with luminous fish
and I thought, "Hey...

3
00:00:10,183 --> 00:00:12,263
...loom."

4
00:00:13,770 --> 00:00:15,940
(Sheldon:)Mom, what are you doing here?

5
00:00:16,106 --> 00:00:17,526
(Mrs Cooper:)Leonard called me.

6
00:00:17,691 --> 00:00:19,821
(Sheldon:)I know, but why?

7
00:00:19,984 --> 00:00:22,444
(Leonard:)Because one of the great minds
of the 21 st century...

8
00:00:22,612 --> 00:00:25,822
(Leonard:)...is raising glow-in-the-dark fish
and weaving serapes.

9
00:00:26,533 --> 00:00:28,783
This is not a serape. This is a poncho.

10
00:00:28,952 --> 00:00:32,122
A serape is open at the sides,
a poncho is closed. This is a poncho.

11
00:00:32,288 --> 00:00:36,418
(Sheldon:)And neither is a reason
to call someone's mother.

12
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:39,250
(Leonard:)Really?
When was the last time you left the house?

13
00:00:40,046 --> 00:00:41,506
(Sheldon:)I went to the market with Penny.

14
00:00:41,673 --> 00:00:43,423
Yeah, that was three weeks ago.

15
00:00:43,591 --> 00:00:44,631
(Sheldon:)Well, then, buckle up.

16
00:00:44,801 --> 00:00:48,891
(Sheldon:)In the next four to eight days,
she's going to get very crabby.

17
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:53,270
(Mrs Cooper:)Sweetheart,
your little friend is concerned about you.

18
00:00:53,435 --> 00:00:54,725
(Sheldon:)Yes, well, I'm not a child.

19
00:00:54,894 --> 00:00:58,024
(Sheldon:)I'm a grown man
capable of living my life as I see fit.

